320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H4
/P 138 0 R
/T (Core idea: instead of measuring statistical randomness \(entropy / chi-squared\), FAV checks whether a file's content still obeys its own format's structural rules \(e.g. a .docx's internal ZIP/XML container\). Even a small amount of encryption breaks those rules -making fine-grained, evasive partial encryption reliably detectable.)
/E (Core idea: instead of measuring statistical randomness \(entropy / chi-squared\), FAV checks whether a file's content still obeys its own format's structural rules \(e.g. a .docx's internal ZIP/XML container\). Even a small amount of encryption breaks those rules -making fine-grained, evasive partial encryption reliably detectable.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [19]
>>
endobj
